This package installs a matched pair of immutable DAPHNE FPGA apps for
`dfx-mgr-client` / `xmutil`:

- `/lib/firmware/xilinx/daphne_selftrigger_ol_<sha7>/`
- `/lib/firmware/xilinx/daphne_fullstream_ol_<sha7>/`

Each app directory contains an app-named `.bin`, an app-named `.dtbo`,
`shell.json`, `BUILD-METADATA.txt`, and a local `SHA256SUMS`. The package also
installs the root-level firmware-name symlink requested by each DTBO. No
mutable `daphne` alias is created; runtime profiles must select the exact app
directory name.

The recipe deliberately fails its fetch task while
`DAPHNE_DUAL_OVERLAY_STAGED = "0"`. The provisioning image excludes this
package and can still parse the layer. Populate both variants atomically with:

```
scripts/petalinux/stage_overlay_into_project.sh \
  /path/to/petalinux-project \
  --self-trigger-output /path/to/selftrigger/output \
  --self-trigger-sha <sha7> \
  --full-stream-output /path/to/fullstream/output \
  --full-stream-sha <sha7>
```

Sources of truth:

- the preferred app-scoped `<app>.SHA256SUMS` from each gateware build (a root
  manifest remains supported for separate legacy output directories)
- the DTBO `firmware-name` property
- `scripts/petalinux/stage_overlay_into_project.sh`

When both bundles are copied into one shared output directory, preserve both
app-scoped manifests. The root `SHA256SUMS` is compatibility output owned by a
single build and may be overwritten by the second packager.
